# Creating and deleting folds (manual method unless a case sets one). Fold state is
# observed through motions: j and k move over a closed fold as if it were one line.

=== zfj creates a closed fold that j moves over
ref:    fold.txt *zf*
quote:  The new fold will be closed for the "manual" method.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
keys:   zfjj
expect:
  one
  two
  |three
  four

=== zf leaves the cursor on the first line of the fold
ref:    fold.txt *zf*
quote:  Operator to create a fold.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
keys:   zfk
expect:
  one
  |two
  three
  four

=== zf2j folds three lines
ref:    fold.txt *zf*
quote:  zf{motion} or {Visual}zf Operator to create a fold.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   zf2jj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
  five

=== zfap folds a paragraph
ref:    fold.txt *zf*
quote:  zf{motion} or {Visual}zf Operator to create a fold.
given:
  |one
  two
  
  four
keys:   zfapj
expect:
  one
  two
  
  |four

=== {Visual}zf folds the selected lines
ref:    fold.txt *zf*
quote:  zf{motion} or {Visual}zf Operator to create a fold.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   Vjzfggjj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
mode:   normal

=== zf sets foldenable
ref:    fold.txt *zf*
quote:  'foldenable' will be set.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   zizfjj
expect:
  one
  two
  |three

=== zF with a count folds that many lines
ref:    fold.txt *zF*
quote:  Create a fold for [count] lines. Works like "zf".
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
keys:   3zFj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four

=== zF without a count folds one line
ref:    fold.txt *zF*
quote:  Create a fold for [count] lines.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   zFj
expect:
  one
  |two
  three

=== :{range}fold creates a closed fold
ref:    fold.txt *:fold*
quote:  Create a fold for the lines in {range}. Works like "zf".
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>jj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four

=== :fold does not move the cursor
ref:    fold.txt *:fold*
quote:  Create a fold for the lines in {range}.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>
expect:
  |one
  two
  three

=== zf over an existing closed fold includes it whole
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When using an operator, a closed fold is included as a whole.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   zfjkzfjzojj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five
  six

=== zd deletes the fold under the cursor
ref:    fold.txt *zd*
quote:  Delete one fold at the cursor. When the cursor is on a folded line, that fold is deleted.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   zfjzdj
expect:
  one
  |two
  three

=== zd moves nested folds one level up
ref:    fold.txt *zd*
quote:  Nested folds are moved one level up.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zdggjjj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five
  six

=== zD deletes nested folds too
ref:    fold.txt *zD*
quote:  Delete folds recursively at the cursor.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zDggjjj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
  five
  six

=== {Visual}zd deletes folds in the selection
ref:    fold.txt *zd*
quote:  In Visual mode one level of all folds (partially) in the selected area are deleted.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>:5,6fold<CR>VGzdggjjjj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five
  six
mode:   normal

=== zE eliminates every fold
ref:    fold.txt *zE*
quote:  Eliminate all folds in the window.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>:5,6fold<CR>zEjjjj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five
  six

=== zd with no fold is an error
ref:    fold.txt *E490*
quote:  All folding commands start with "z".
given:
  |one
  two
keys:   zd
expect:
  |one
  two
msg:    E490: No fold found

=== zf with foldmethod indent is an error
ref:    fold.txt *zf*
quote:  This only works when 'foldmethod' is "manual" or "marker".
given:
  |one
  two
keys:   :set fdm=indent<CR>zfj
expect:
  one
  |two
msg:    E350: Cannot create fold with current 'foldmethod'

=== zE with foldmethod indent is an error
ref:    fold.txt *zE*
quote:  This only works when 'foldmethod' is "manual" or "marker".
given:
  |one
  two
keys:   :set fdm=indent<CR>zE
expect:
  |one
  two
msg:    E352: Cannot erase folds with current 'foldmethod'

=== zf with foldmethod marker appends markers
ref:    fold.txt *fold-create-marker*
quote:  Vim will append the start and end marker, as specified with 'foldmarker'. The markers are appended to the end of the line.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   :set fdm=marker<CR>zfj
expect:
  |one{{{
  two}}}
  three

=== zd with foldmethod marker removes the markers
ref:    fold.txt *fold-delete-marker*
quote:  "\"zd\" can be used to delete a fold defined by markers.  Vim will delete the markers for you."
given:
  |one{{{
  two}}}
  three
keys:   :set fdm=marker<CR>zd
expect:
  |one
  two
  three
